Container"><span class="Formatted"><b>Wow, this had a wild start all the way to the end. </b> <br><b>
  <a href="www.booktrovertreader.com" rel="nofollow noopener">I have many thoughts on this book....</a>
</b><br><br>Officially making plans to read Danielle Jensen's backlog of books<br><br><img src="https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1735752593i/36350958._SX540_.png" width="200" height="170" alt="" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><b>Read My Honest Book Review on My Blog:</b> <a href="https://booktrovertreader.com/honest-review-of-the-bridge-kingdom/" rel="nofollow noopener"> <br>The Bridge Kingdom</a><br><br>There was one point in this story that 90% of me was thinking to myself "This is a little too happy." Then <b> WHAM </b> crap hits the fan and Danielle pulls the rug from underneath you and gives you a solid ending. <br><br>This was a cool story. The FMC is really tough as nuts and is a BA in this. Not just all bark and no bite. Our FMC Lara can fight without hesitation. I wish I saw more of her assassin abilities in this one but there is a good chance I will see it in the next book for reasons that I won't say.<br><br>The story did drag a bit in between 60-80%. Lara was getting comfortable with her new world and with her new husband. But it got a little mundane and I almost wasn't enjoying it for a bit there.<br><br>I cannot wait to read the next one because this one slightly left me hanging.<br><br><b>Connect With Me:</b><br><br><b><a href="www.booktrovertreader.com" rel="nofollow noopener">BLOG</a> ⟫ <a href="https://www.instagram.com/booktrovertreader/" rel="nofollow noopener">INSTAGRAM</a> ⟫ <a href="https://booktrovert-reader.ck.page/3a8ba82372" rel="nofollow noopener">NEWSLETTER</a> ⟫<br></b></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__lab