/span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">3.5* rounded up<br /><br />Audiobook narrated by Lauren Fortgang and James Patrick Cronin<br /><br />I have 50 unfinished series. So what, the number is always n-1, n being the actual number of series that I need to read. So, here I am finishing the 1st volume from yet another Romantasy series. It seems like I am enjoying them a little bit too much these days. <br /><br />The Bridge Kingdom has the enemy to lovers trope. Lara has prepared all her life to become the future bride of King Aren of The Bridge Kingdom. Also, she was trained hundreds of ways to kill him and to destroy his realm. When she finally becomes his bride, she realises that the king might not be really the monster Lara’s father made her believe to be. Obviously, feelings become to change, blah blah<br /><br />There is nothing extraordinary or new about this series. However, the writing is decent, characters are interesting enough and I plan to read the next one as well, see where it takes me.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/22189348?shelf=fantasy-sf" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">fantasy-sf</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/22189348?shelf=romance" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">romance</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued">