.gr.book.v3.zS1xyR4PN9o4dVbP","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.zS1xyR4PN9o4dVbP"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/40997852?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"2020","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/40997852?shelf=2020"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"fantasy","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/40997852?shelf=fantasy"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"romance","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/40997852?shelf=romance"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"new-adult","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/40997852?shelf=new-adult"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3594491395"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.D8OMs0yx6JoCy9h2EE37BA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.D8OMs0yx6JoCy9h2EE37BA","creator":{"__ref":"User:40997852"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1785734373106,"createdAt":1604775864606,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1779012048820,"text":"On the surface, this is a story many of us seek. Enemies to lovers. She’s trained her whole life to be the downfall of her future husband’s kingdom. Betrothed because of a treaty, Lara is sent to marry the evil king of the bridge kingdom. She needs to discover the secrets of the important bridge connecting the continents, its weaknesses, and of course, any flaws that might help take it over. Several kingdoms tried from the outside and failed constantly. Her people are starving because Ithicana is monopolizing trade. \u003cbr /\u003eHaving been trained all her life as an assassin, a spy, and in a way, a queen, Lara didn’t expect to actually like the people of her new kingdom, they were supposed to be evil, you know?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWhile I wouldn’t say it’s the most innovative plotline, if done well, I enjoy it immensely. I was looking for a book similar to \u003ca href=\"https://goodreads.com/book/show/52831200.From_Blood_and_Ash__Blood_and_Ash___1_\" title=\"From Blood and Ash (Blood and Ash, #1) by Jennifer L. Armentrout\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eFrom Blood and Ash\u003c/a\u003e but sadly, this one wasn’t nearly as good. I was willing to ignore the boring cover because I’ve learned a long time ago to not judge books by their covers but in this case, the book is actually as dull as its cover.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWhile I was considering rating this 3 stars, I was looking for any element in this book that might help. I found none. The most interesting thing happened on the last page and made me think of reading the sequel but of course, I won’t.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWhy didn’t I like this book you might be wondering?\u003cbr /\u003eWell, \u003cb\u003ethe characters are so meh\u003c/b\u003e. Especially Aren. While Lara was ok at first, Aren didn’t impress me. Don’t get me wrong, I didn’t \u003ci\u003edislike\u003c/i\u003e them but didn’t care for them either. I couldn’t feel the sexual tension nor the burning chemistry. You’d think that almost nothing happening between the characters until 80% might help. It didn’t. They were bland. And of course, I wasn’t reading this book for the world-building. I was reading it for the romance (NA style in a fantasy world). Oh well.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eI also found the world-building lacking.\u003c/b\u003e Yes, we got lots of info about Icathana but I wish we knew more about the other kingdoms, their cultures, and how developed they were. This didn’t affect my rating because maybe even we did, I wouldn’t have been interested. Maybe.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFurthermore, \u003cb\u003eI found the behavior of the main characters questionable. \u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFor example, Aren, defending her and choosing her over people who back him up. Like dude, you know her for one month tops, she is the child of your former enemy, while those people would die for you… He trusted her too easily. \u003cbr /\u003eI won’t talk about Lara because I’d be spoiling it but I’m not sure if it counts as such because the \u003cu\u003ePLOT WAS SO OBVIOUS\u003c/u\u003e. I predicted what’s going to happen from the start and I was thinking if doesn’t, I’ll give it 3 stars. Sadly, I’ve read too many books to not guess but it doesn’t take a genius to guess. \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"bdf0c9c5-6141-4dbb-98e9-57aa33d0791e\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"bdf0c9c5-6141-4dbb-98e9-57aa33d0791e\"\u003eI hate that she wasn’t truthful with him. why didn’t Lara at least tell him about her sisters? Why didn’t she frankly explain what she tried to do? This was painfully obvious that it’s going to be sent even if she didn’t want it to.\u003cbr /\u003eAnother thing is Lara trusting her father too much. When I heard Aren saying “they’ll starve before they see any benefit from this treaty” (or something along these lines), I knew it’s the father who’s the bad guy. While she couldn’t investigate a bit for her own when everything told her otherwise? Her father who treated her horribly suddenly cares about his people? \u003c/label\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI’ll keep this short and sum it up by this:\u003cbr /\u003eYou might enjoy it. Many enjoyed this book. I really wanted to like but it ended up boring and painfully predictable with one-dimensional characters. The secondary ones were actually decent and I would’ve liked to know more \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"f980e9f7-ed93-431c-b628-9da98818e9dd\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"f980e9f7-ed93-431c-b628-9da98818e9dd\"\u003esister\u003c/label\u003e but I don’t think it’ll make reading Traitor Queen much better. I wish we had more dynamics between the main characters and well, more depth to the story. It had potential but it wasn’t for me.","rating":2,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2VCMCYHGBNNIW\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.zS1xyR4PN9o4dVbP\"}}"},"likeCount":517,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":60},"User:39575951":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":39575951,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1460553725i/39575951._UX200_CR0,10,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":1777,"textReviewsCount":510,"name":"Felix (Helen 2.0)","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/39575951-felix-helen-2-0","contributor":null,"id":39575951},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A29PMRJF2TM46T":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A29PMRJF2TM46T"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A29PMRJF2TM46T\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.GBnO9cdTV3QfRiFpvYtnBQ\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A29PMRJF2TM46T","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A29PMRJF2TM46T"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.GBnO9cdTV3QfRiFpvYtnBQ","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.GBnO9cdTV3QfRiFpvYtnBQ"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/39575951?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"romantasy","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/39575951?shelf=romantasy"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"royalty","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/39575951?shelf=royalty"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"enemies-to-lovers","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/39575951?shelf=enemies-to-lovers"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"spies-assassins","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/39575951?shelf=spies-assassins"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"contract-marriage","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/39575951?shelf=contract-marriage"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"support-womens-wrongs","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/39575951?shelf=support-womens-wrongs"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"anti-heroine","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/39575951?shelf=anti-heroine"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"warrior-mc","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/39575951?shelf=warrior-mc"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"new-adult","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/39575951?shelf=new-adult"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"pov-dual","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/39575951?shelf=pov-dual"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5600832240"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.ShyT-g4vxrM7lahtRJycYw":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.ShyT-g4vxrM7lahtRJycYw","creator":{"__ref":"User:39575951"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1785677360504,"createdAt":1694896510704,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1714048595211,"text":"This is the kind of book where you shouldn’t pause and think about what’s happening while you’re reading or it might ruin the experience for you when you realize that none of the world building or plot makes any sense. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eIf you close one eye and take everything 100% at face value, I think there’s a good chance you can enjoy this book.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eIt’s not *bad* per se but I do think lots of the book was constructed more for the ✨vibes✨ than anything substantive. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe plot opens on a sort of “last supper” of twelve princess sisters dining with their dad, the king. The princesses have been locked away in the desert all their lives, training to become assassin spies. One of them will marry the King Aren of Ithicana, the enemy kingdom, and send all his secrets back to their father. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSo the king’s plan, now that it’s finally time for one princess to marry Aren, is to pick the best of his twelve surviving daughters (he started with twenty) and have the rest killed. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis is a really stupid plan. What if your one chosen daughter catches the flu three days later and dies? Poof, there goes decades of your work. Shouldn’t you at least keep one spare on hand? Also, wtf does he even gain by killing the rest? If they haven’t spilled his secrets while trapped in the desert so far, why would they start now? \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eClearly this whole “kill the daughters” plot point is just for shock value and to make extra extra sure that the readers understand this dad is SUPER DUPER EVIL. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBecause, you know, forcing all your daughters to endure decades of torturous training in the desert then selling them off to your enemies isn’t evil enough. The silly readers might get confused and accidentally like this guy! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSo the FMC, Lara, is the princess who makes the cut and gets married off to Ithicana. She’s hellbent on finding a way to destroy her new husband and his kingdom by finding a gap in their defenses which will allow her dad’s army to invade and slaughter the Ithicanians. This, because she thinks Aren’s tough trade tax policies are causing her people back home to starve. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWhy does she believe this? Because her evil dad told her so. He told her he’s just so dedicated to helping his poor people who are suffering under those darn Ithicanian trade taxes. She takes this at full face value, since we all know evil child-murdering fathers are trustworthy and have only the most benevolent of intentions. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eNow, if you, unlike Lara, have more than two braincells, you might have guessed the big twist here already—it’s actually her dad whose shitty policies are leading their people to starve!! Shocking!! I expected so much better out of a child murderer! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI figured this out at maybe 3-4 chapters in. For Lara, it takes 75% of the book. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSure, she grew up to some degree brainwashed, but she clearly knows enough to understand that the way she and her sisters were raised was wrong and fucked up. If you get that, how do you not take the tiniest step forward in logic to understand that the evil people who raised you might just be LIARS?!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSpending most of the book watching Lara make stupid decisions based on stupid assumptions that \u003ci\u003ewill lead to the massacre of the Ithicanian people she now rules\u003c/i\u003e was a tad frustrating.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe rest of the plot was equally predictable if you’re at all familiar with romantasy tropes. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAs for the romance, I could see how some people might enjoy it, but it wasn’t very meaningful to me. Aren, the love interest, might as well have been a cardboard box with some eyes and abs drawn on it. His one personality trait was being into Lara.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSo basically this was one big meh-fest for me. I might try book 2, I might not.","rating":2,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A29PMRJF2TM46T\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.GBnO9cdTV3QfRiFpvYtnBQ\"}}"},"likeCount":430,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":39},"User:26262267":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":26262267,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1578858809i/26262267._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":849,"textReviewsCount":451,"name":"• Lindsey Dahling •","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/26262267-lindsey-dahling","contributor":null,"id":26262267},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2LV7OSOZHNBJ1":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2LV7OSOZHNBJ1"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2LV7OSOZHNBJ1\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.GBnO9cdTV3QfRiFpvYtnBQ\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A2LV7OSOZHNBJ1","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A2LV7OSOZHNBJ1"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.GBnO9cdTV3QfRiFpvYtnBQ","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.GBnO9cdTV3QfRiFpvYtnBQ"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/26262267?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"this-book-is-bitchin","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/26262267?shelf=this-book-is-bitchin"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"book-club","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/26262267?shelf=book-club"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3275579447"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.HQZGrHin02DHYEWlzBJT9w":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.HQZGrHin02DHYEWlzBJT9w","creator":{"__ref":"User:26262267"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1784798082813,"createdAt":1590480523435,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1590519576804,"text":"If you’re a fan of the \u003ci\u003eA Court of Thorns and Roses\u003c/i\u003e series and/or \u003ci\u003eThe Bargainer\u003c/i\u003e series, drop everything you’re doing AND READ THIS BOOK RIGHT FUCKING NOW.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eNOT KIDDING. RIGHT NOW. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI can’t even tell you why because spoilers. Just trust me. TRUST ME, OKAY. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI just finished it and my heart is still racing. I can’t handle it. IT WAS SO GOOD. It doesn’t have Fae or magic or any elements like that in it, but you ACOTAR/Bargainer/good book fans especially NEED TO READ IT BECAUSE OMGGGGGGG.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFOCUS, LINDSEY. FOCUS.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eHOKAY.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e1. Likable characters galore.\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSERIOUSLY. I am in love with just about EVERYONE in this book (which is a damn miracle because in real life I don’t like anyone). I want to be their friend. I want to be their family member. I WANT TO BE THEM. (Not in a creepy, stalkerish way.) (I’m aware saying that doesn’t help my case.)\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e2. THE FUCKING SLOW BURN IS HOLY SHIT.\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSo excellent that I can’t even form proper sentences. I just 😏😏😏😏😏😏😏\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e3. Badass characters all over the place.\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe MC, Lara, especially. Goddamn. The woman is lethal. She’s not a delicate flower. Get the hell out of her way. Hello, Lara. I’m here. Please take my heart and soul.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e4. The author doesn’t drag her feet when it comes to plot.\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis book hits the ground running in the first chapter. You’re catapulted right into the action. THAT is how it should be done. Had my attention from cover to cover. I can honestly say there were no boring parts for me. The author knows when to go into detail and when to sort of gloss over weeks of nothing happening. I’m a fan of that. I have a hard time reading books where the goal is to get on a ship and sail to another country and conquer it, but it takes half the damn book to get there (or, you know, never happens in Daenerys Targaryen’s case—moron). Especially when nothing really happens on the ship. This book doesn’t waste time on that. If nothing happens during the “sailing” time, she just says something like, “Three weeks later, we arrived.” Love that type of storytelling. It focuses on character development and action. It doesn’t waste time on irrelevant events/characters. Which, in my opinion, is the way it SHOULD be. 💯👏🏻 (Sorry, Charles Dickens.)\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e5. It made me FEEL things.\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI laughed out loud at the banter. I was positively giddy during slow burn interactions. I felt stressed AF while certain conflicts played out. I even teared up at a few parts. GUYS. I AM SUPPOSED TO BE DEAD INSIDE. WHAT HAS THIS BOOK DONE TO ME?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eAm I going to read the sequel?\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eGurl you already know the answer to this. (Cue heavy breathing cat meme)","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2LV7OSOZHNBJ1\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.GBnO9cdTV3QfRiFpvYtnBQ\"}}"},"likeCount":417,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":76},"User:127632948":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":127632948,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1729856926i/127632948._UX200_CR0,25,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":3523,"textReviewsCount":909,"name":"Clace ","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/127632948-clace","contributor":null,"id":127632948},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A5AXPSHC1RMFP":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A5AXPSHC1RMFP"},"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.2GImujBahAsqPWom":{"__typename":"Book","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.2GImujBahAsqPWom"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A5AXPSHC1RMFP\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.2GImujBahAsqPWom\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A5AXPSHC1RMFP","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A5AXPSHC1RMFP"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.2GImujBahAsqPWom","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.2GImujBahAsqPWom"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/127632948?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"the-bane-of-my-existence","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/127632948?shelf=the-bane-of-my-existence"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/7775222491"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.eDdgylMHuS_RHZwpcK55BA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.eDdgylMHuS_RHZwpcK55BA","creator":{"__ref":"User:127632948"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1785098777240,"createdAt":1753609102213,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1754739676476,"text":"\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e5 stars!!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\"Since the moment I set eyes on you in Southwatch, there's been no one but you. Even if I'm a goddamned fool for it, there will never be anyone but you\"\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eDanielle L. Jensen has never disappointed me ever! I was always recommended this series, and I knew it would be amazing. Before this, I read one of her series \u003ci\u003eDark Shores\u003c/i\u003e, which had me obsessed, so I just had to read this, and oh boy, how glad I am to have read this because it was everything that I was hoping for. This series deserves \u003cb\u003eso much more hype and love because it's quite literally perfect\u003c/b\u003e. It's not overburdening with its length as most fantasies are; within just 300-330 pages for both books, it captures what it intends to execute perfectly, and I just love how she made all these 300 pages count without dragging or rushing the story. Besides that is the fact how \u003cb\u003eatmospheric\u003c/b\u003e her writing is \u003cb\u003eimmersive\u003c/b\u003e, like she writes, and I'm fully immersed in it. I just have this vivid imagination of the entire setting, and I am in love. Her writing is very fast-paced, and each chapter ends with a cliffhanger, not letting you stop. I kept on saying one more chapter till the book was finished because the stakes were sky high from the start to the finish.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e“This man might be a hunter. But he was mistaken if he believed she was prey.”\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eLara\u003c/b\u003e, stunned me so bad! I had no idea that I was about to read about an FMC who was this cunning, manipulative, and strong 😋. It was honestly such a breath of fresh air to be in her mind because it was so unique and well thought off, I loved how all her actions were pre planned, well though and perfectly executed, Her strive for what she wanted and the determination that she had was so inspiring, the way she could seduce and manipulate cards in her favour was something that had me in awe the entire time, I loved how well trained she was and how she tried to look past the brainwashed memories and fought against her mind. One thing that sat right with me was that despite her wicked cleverness, sharp wit, strength, and determination, she always found out what was right and tried to be on that side 🙂‍↕️.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e“She was so painfully beautiful, and even knowing that she'd used it against him didn't lessen how powerfully he was drawn to her.”\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eAren\u003c/b\u003e, he was so badly whipped for Lara 😭 like that man was so in love with her. At first, I was a bit taken aback by how easily Aren was able to trust Lara. Well, it did take a lot of time since there were time jumps, but I feel like it's also because we were made to believe that Ithicanians were barbarian's and this proved that they're not. They are people who care and love and are just trying to protect their own. I loved how determined he was to protect his people. I liked how far he was willing to go for that. Aren is being torn apart for his people, and Lara was so fun to see. I also loved seeing the progress of how he viewed Lara and eventually how deeply he fell in love because after the betrayal ( which is very obvious and not a spoiler), he was insanely mad at her, BUT still defended her. A man a ma-ma-ma-man.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e“I love you,\" he said, his lips grazing against hers. \"And I will love you, no matter what the future brings. No matter how hard I need to fight. I will always love you.\"\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eRomance\u003c/b\u003e, I knew this was a tragic romance from the start, because this quite literally starts with betrayal set in the future under the circumstances that they meet in. It wasn't a slow burn, but it also was a slow burn?? I liked that it wasn't insta-lusty. The yearning was 🫦, the chemistry was 😋, and the tension was 🥵. I honestly cannot remember the last time I was this hooked on a book where I was invested in every single aspect, like I knew that this romance wasn't going to end well, but Danielle made me fall in love with it, and it hurt so much!! I loved their bickering and banter, and I was getting so fond of that, but ughh, what I was dreading the most happened, and no matter how hard I tried to prepare myself, it still shook the earth from below my feet.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e\"I will be the next Queen of Ithicana. And I will bring the Bridge Kingdom to its knees.\"\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eThe plot and the worldbuilding\u003c/b\u003e, the plot was so well set, it was perfectly in motion to what Danielle had in mind because the way it starts with overthrowing a kingdom and then expands into something more with newer characters being introduced and how it follows in book 2 with it reaching a new peak was amazing, the world building was nice, the war tides concept was very fun to read about, I just know I cant live in Ithicana because of their snake problem but I loved the difference in Madriana and Ithicana and how distinct they are, I also loved how the politics were weaved through this because that made it read more like an actual fantasy rather than a romantasy.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eThe ending\u003c/b\u003e was the most torturous thing that I have read. Betrayal after betrayal after betrayal. Twists after twists after twists. I am unwell!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e“Ithicana—and its king—bent to nothing and no one. But he bent for her.”\u003c/i\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e__\u003cbr /\u003eI absolutely loved every other work of Danielle, especially \u003ci\u003e'Dark shores'\u003c/i\u003e. Everyone has always recommended this one, saying it's the best, and my sisters have also hyped it up for me so much! I have to start it now!!","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A5AXPSHC1RMFP\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.2GImujBahAsqPWom\"}}"},"likeCount":339,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":82},"User:84801697":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":84801697,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1646081976i/84801697._UY200_CR35,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":3805,"textReviewsCount":1388,"name":"Lucie V.","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/84801697-lucie-v","contributor":null,"id":84801697},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/ADJY0EK94H1RO":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/ADJY0EK94H1RO"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/ADJY0EK94H1RO\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.CeCnfu2hDLOWGucm\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/ADJY0EK94H1RO","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/ADJY0EK94H1RO"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.CeCnfu2hDLOWGucm","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.CeCnfu2hDLOWGucm"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/84801697?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"fantasy","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/84801697?shelf=fantasy"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"favorites","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/84801697?shelf=favorites"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"hate-to-love","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/84801697?shelf=hate-to-love"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"arranged-marriage","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/84801697?shelf=arranged-marriage"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"audiobooks","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/84801697?shelf=audiobooks"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3092085305"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.--hXNMuhcIhfELLYZuin_A":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.--hXNMuhcIhfELLYZuin_A","creator":{"__ref":"User:84801697"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1778076486718,"createdAt":1596405013726,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1772461478443,"text":"✅ Only one bed trope\u003cbr /\u003e✅ “Who did this to you?”\u003cbr /\u003e✅ Arranged marriage \u003cbr /\u003e✅ Hate-to-love\u003cbr /\u003e✅ 2 POVs\u003cbr /\u003e✅ Badass and ruthless main characters \u003cbr /\u003e✅ World-building\u003cbr /\u003e✅ Slow burn romance\u003cbr /\u003e✅ Action and fighting\u003cbr /\u003e✅ Politics and spying\u003cbr /\u003e❗️❗️ Cliffhanger\u003cbr /\u003e❗️❗️ Trigger warnings: child abuse, drugging, murders, war and mild gore, use of narcotics on others, violence, shark attacks\u003cbr /\u003e🔥 Spice level : 🌶️🌶️🌶️ / 5\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e_______________________ \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eThird read/listen:\u003c/b\u003e Still as good as the first 2 times. I can't wait to reread the angst-fest that is the second book!\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e_______________________ \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003e\n    \u003ci\u003eThere would be no happily-ever-after. Not for her.\u003c/i\u003e\n  \u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eI adore hate-to-love stories, and this one is great!\u003c/b\u003e Add to that an arranged marriage, a country made of deadly islands full of serpents, sharks, and violent storms, a strong badass heroine, and a kind but fierce male lead, and you've got yourself a pretty epic adventure. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003e\n    \u003ci\u003e“You murdered your sisters for the good of our country?” His voice was amused.\u003cbr /\u003eLara forced a chuckle from her lips. “Hardly. I murdered them because I wished to live.”\u003c/i\u003e\n  \u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eLara Veliant is a princess of Maridrina, one of many daughters of the cruel King Silas. She was raised to be a ruthless assassin since she was 5, so her father could send her to marry the new king of Ithicana as part of an old peace treaty. He expects her to find out how to take control of the famous bridge of Ithicana, thus helping Maridrina get revenge on Ithicana and ensure their prosperity. Whoever controls the bridge controls the commerce between the north and the south and Lara is determined to save her people from their misery. Lara is also expected to kill her husband when the time comes, and she is more than willing to do it for her country. Lara does not care for her coldhearted father, but she does care for her people who are starving. She also wishes to gain her freedom from her father, and he promised to let her go free once she fulfills her purpose. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003e\n    \u003ci\u003eAll she had ever known was violence. It was nothing to her. And everything.\u003c/i\u003e\n  \u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eThe beginning of this book is so intense and shows how ruthless Lara is!\u003c/b\u003e She is driven and determined to do whatever it takes to survive and protect the few persons she loves. Her father cares only about his power and is willing to kill whoever stands in the way of his plans, or whoever is even aware of the plans because he needs to cover his tracks. Lara is shipped to Ithicana where she expects to hate her cruel husband but she discovers a dangerous and wonderful land, ruled by a kind but fierce king and she soon realizes that her father and tutors may have not told her the truth about the situation in Maridrina and Ithicana.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003e\n    \u003ci\u003e\"I wanted to see the bridge.\"\u003cbr /\u003eAren stopped in his tracks, turning to give her a sharp look. \"Why?\"\u003cbr /\u003eShe met his gaze unflinchingly. \"I wanted to see the bit of architecture that was worth the right to my body. My loyalty. My life.\"\u003cbr /\u003eHe recoiled as though she'd slapped him. \"The rights to those things are yours to give, not your father's.\" \u003c/i\u003e\n  \u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eThe kingdom of Ithicana is a magical, dangerous, and unforgiving land.\u003c/b\u003e The world-building is vivid and intricate, and the descriptions are superb. It is very easy to lose ourselves in this book and to picture what life in Ithicana entails, and I absolutely adore the atmosphere and world the author created in this book.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003e\n    \u003ci\u003e She was so painfully beautiful, and even knowing that she'd used it against him didn't lessen how powerfully he was drawn to her. \u003c/i\u003e\n  \u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAren Kertell is the 37th King of Ithicana and Lara's soon-to-be husband. Ithicana survives with the money it makes from the bridge that crosses their kingdom. The bridge allows trade between neighboring kingdoms, and whoever controls the bridge controls the trade. The kingdom is made of many islands, all more dangerous than the other. They have hungry sharks, snakes, violent storms, dangerous waters, and jungles full of predators. It's a good thing that Lara is strong and can take care of herself, even if she needs to hide it and pretend that she is mostly defenseless.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003e\n    \u003ci\u003eThis man might be a hunter. But he was mistaken if he believed she was prey.\u003c/i\u003e\n  \u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eThe romance is slow to build but smooth, sweet, and realistic. \u003c/b\u003eLara needs to appear as a demure, fragile, and non-threatening young woman, but she is deadly. Arren wants nothing to do with her since he suspects that she might be there to spy on him and just doesn't want a wife right now, but the sexual tension between them is there from the start. There are some steamy moments and they are just swoon-worthy together. I like that despite their physical attraction to each other, Lara remained focused on her mission until she was forced to admit that her father had lied to her. The same goes for Aren, even though he thought Lara to be a fragile but gorgeous flower, he still managed to keep her at arm’s length because he knew that trusting her without undeniable proof of her loyalty would be stupid.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003e\n    \u003ci\u003eShe wanted to stay, to fight and sweat and bleed for him and his harsh, wild, and beautiful kingdom.\u003c/i\u003e\n  \u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe political plot to ruin Ithicana and give Maridrina control over the bridge is a big part of the story and I really liked to see how Lara was struggling because she didn't know who to help and who to trust. She was not easily swayed just because the king is young and gorgeous instead of being an old cruel man, but she quickly realized that Aren was kind and selfless when it came to his kingdom. He is far from the demon-like king Lara's father described, and she found herself stuck between a rock and a hard place because she has to choose between gaining her freedom by betraying Aren or following her heart and her conscience by remaining with him, but knowing that her father would find her and kill her sooner or later if she failed her mission. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAs she learns the harsh truth about her father, and as she sees that the people of Ithicana are constantly fighting to survive, Lara has a tough choice to make. She needs to decide if she will fight for Maridrina or Ithicana, because helping Maridrina will come at the cost of Ithicana’s destruction, and much to Lara’s surprise, she has come to love this harsh land and its brave and loyal people.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003e\n    \u003ci\u003e\"Everything you’ve said, everything you’ve done, everything between us has been a damned lie.\"\u003c/i\u003e\n  \u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eThe pace is perfect and engaging, but also slow enough to leave room for relationship-building and character growth, and the plot is well-developed, full of action, and keeps us at the edge of our seats. \u003c/b\u003eWe are thrown into the action from chapter one, and it just never stops being engaging and compelling. The spying part is full of stressful moments, the action scenes are well done, and the romance is a slow-burn enemies to lovers. I truly loved everything about this book.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI definitely recommend this book if you like strong main characters, steamy hate-to-love romance, politics, and spying games, with a lot of life-or-death situations and a few twists. Also, the way the book ends promises a lot of angst for the second book, I cannot wait to read it! \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.instagram.com/lucie_v_booklover/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eFollow me on Instagram\u003c/a\u003e 🙂","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/ADJY0EK94H1RO\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.CeCnfu2hDLOWGucm\"}}"},"likeCount":278,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":15},"User:90586539":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":90586539,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1763254562i/90586539._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":9533,"textReviewsCount":389,"name":"Ali L","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/90586539-ali-l","contributor":null,"id":90586539},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A11GCY5L7ZZ5RL":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A11GCY5L7ZZ5RL"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A11GCY5L7ZZ5RL\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.CeCnfu2hDLOWGucm\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A11GCY5L7ZZ5RL","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A11GCY5L7ZZ5RL"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.CeCnfu2hDLOWGucm","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.CeCnfu2hDLOWGucm"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/90586539?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/6034563249"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.ycRjfswykOVPunUyxzUzNQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.ycRjfswykOVPunUyxzUzNQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:90586539"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1785207525917,"createdAt":1732466474079,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1732479470717,"text":"A young princess is married off to a neighboring king and proceeds to drug absolutely everybody she meets. Her new husband is sort of the human version of a resigned, duty-bound sigh, but he’s a very important man (he has a bridge). She has this whole plan to take down his kingdom from the inside so she can save her people but he’s like, really hot and nice and probably has a facial scar that makes him look dashing (I might have made that part up) so really what choice does she have? The supporting cast is primarily a series of little islands that feature a lot of snakes. This is marketed as a fantasy, despite not having any typical fantasy elements like magic, fae, or mythical creatures, but maybe that’s an easier sell to the masses than “book about the geopolitical consequences of government-driven artificial scarcity propaganda and realistic examination of marriage as a form of allegiance between formally warring factions”, I don’t know. Also there are sharks!","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A11GCY5L7ZZ5RL\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.CeCnfu2hDLOWGucm\"}}"},"likeCount":271,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":6},"User:142072672":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":142072672,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1771305547i/142072672._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":13007,"textReviewsCount":644,"name":"SK ","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/142072672-sk","contributor":null,"id":142072672},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3654WU95SBAAX":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3654WU95SBAAX"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3654WU95SBAAX\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.zS1xyR4PN9o4dVbP\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3654WU95SBAAX","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3654WU95SBAAX"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.zS1xyR4PN9o4dVbP","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.zS1xyR4PN9o4dVbP"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/142072672?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4361914512"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.xvYZarolQSnE-MWHiYxRlQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.xvYZarolQSnE-MWHiYxRlQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:142072672"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1785129296559,"createdAt":1655455158258,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1655535494403,"text":"\"She would fight for him.\u003cbr /\u003eShe would bleed for him. \u003cbr /\u003eShe would die for him.\" \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eMy mind is blown. I seriously did not expect it to be THIS good. You all were not lying. The last few chapters and the cliffhanger were so brutal. I was literally reading it with tears in my eyes😭😭 I'm going to need Danielle Jensen pay for my therapy.... \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe plot is amazing. It doesn't have any supernatural beings but it's so damn interesting, it's hard not to get lost in this fantasy world. The world building is done beautifully and it's easy to keep track of. The characters are total badass. I did not see certain plot twists coming and that kept the element of surprise, which I seriously enjoyed. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAren and Lara are so easy to love. Both of them as individuals are full of personality and independency. They don't need to rely on each other to win their battles. As a couple? They're unbeatable. The way Aren was smitten by her since the beginning was so sweet to see and the way Lara opened up to him was just chef's kiss 🤌 I liked how the both of them will do anything to protect the other. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe supporting characters are equally good.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAs you can tell by now, I'm completely in love with this book and everything about it. So, of course I HIGHLY RECOMMEND it. You guys, don't hesitate to pick this one up. I can't wait to start with The Traitor Queen 😩\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThanks to my girl, @Leonie for making me read this.... Again with the good recs lol🙈♥️","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3654WU95SBAAX\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.zS1xyR4PN9o4dVbP\"}}"},"likeCount":240,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":53},"User:101179363":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":101179363,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1783051999i/101179363._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":3226,"textReviewsCount":528,"name":"₊  ˚  ale   ࿓ ♡ ⋆｡˚","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/101179363-ale","contributor":null,"id":101179363},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A10KEMNOUSJKOY":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A10KEMNOUSJKOY"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A10KEMNOUSJKOY\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.GBnO9cdTV3QfRiFpvYtnBQ\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A10KEMNOUSJKOY","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A10KEMNOUSJKOY"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.GBnO9cdTV3QfRiFpvYtnBQ","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.GBnO9cdTV3QfRiFpvYtnBQ"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/101179363?shelf=read"},"taggings":[{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"favorites","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/101179363?shelf=favorites"}},{"__typename":"Tagging","tag":{"__typename":"Tag","name":"series","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/101179363?shelf=series"}}],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3824168997"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.92TGMJ5D562gPmXEpPyhiQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.92TGMJ5D562gPmXEpPyhiQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:101179363"},"recommendFor":"Everyone. This is a book that all the GR community must read. It's a treasure.","updatedAt":1767544138978,"createdAt":1619584778077,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1619628423097,"text":"\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003cblockquote\u003e“Even if I'm a goddamned fool for it, there will never be anyone but you.”\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eHello, you, yes, you, who is reading this and looking for a good fantasy book, romance, action, with forced marriage and enemies to lovers, with a giant cat, a world divided by a bridge, islands with snakes, jungles, a grandmother obsessed with people's teeth, killer princesses and a handsome and sweet king.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eLook no further. The Bridge Kingdom is that, and more. My old and wicked heart fell in love with this book. It is perfect and has a little bit of everything.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI must admit I had a hard time finishing this book because I was always busy with college hanging over me, and ended up procrastinating. But yesterday I read more than half of the book to completion, and I am satisfied with my decision to read it just yesterday.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThere are spoilers, I guess, so, watch out, y'all.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eLara and her sisters were raised to be spies and assassins, they have been trained to defend themselves, and to kill the king of Ithicana, whom one of them will marry, spy on, and send the king of Madririna information to attack Ithicana, who owns the Bridge. Lara poisons her sisters, although it is more a sedative so that none of them is condemned and dies: she sacrifices herself for them.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eLara marries the king of Ithicana, Aren. She has lived being fed by a hatred directed towards him, and later she realizes that it is an unjustified hatred and full of lies. Something totally false. At first, Lara despises Aren and tries to find Ithicana's secrets to send to her father, the king of Madririna.\u003cbr\u003eThey end up falling in love. Aren realizes that Lara is a spy, and proves to her that the king of Madririna has been lying to his daughter all this time, that he filled her head with lies and false promises just to get the Bridge.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe most predictable thing about the book is known from the beginning, and it's not a bad thing: we know it's all going to go to shit at any moment. My anxiety wouldn't let me live because every now and then I kept telling myself, \"this is going to go to hell very soon.\" And I was expecting it, in many action-packed and intense scenes.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cu\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003ePlot.\u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/u\u003e\u003cbr\u003eFrom the moment you read the synopsis, you know it's going to be good; it grabs you. The pace is quite addictive, so much so, that you don't even feel the chapters; you just want to keep reading. There are many plot twists that I didn't see coming, and several minor ones that I did, but they weren't that relevant tbh.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cu\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003eWriting.\u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/u\u003e\u003cbr\u003eOh gods, the writing is perfect; it's not complicated and it doesn't try to describe difficult things either. Even the smut scenes were divine and well told; SJM and JLA, this goes for you. There was nothing forced about the tension between Aren and Lara, and I just wanted to scream at them to kiss already, because even I couldn't handle the tension between those two, which was fantastic and quite entertaining.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cu\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003eWorldbuilding.\u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/u\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThe book doesn't come with a map, so it was a little bit hard for me to get my bearings at first, and in the review by the amazing \u003ca href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/3665046323\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eMarta\u003c/a\u003e, there is a nice \u003ca href=\"https://cdnb.artstation.com/p/assets/images/images/028/157/997/large/damien-mammoliti-bridgekingdom-worldmap-cities.jpg?1593637594\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003emap\u003c/a\u003e that helps you understand the kingdoms and their locations. It's amazing - they're islands! Most fantasy books portray run-of-the-mill kingdoms with snowfall and such, Ithicana has storms and an aggressive sea that keeps its enemies at bay.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cu\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003eCharacters.\u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/u\u003e\u003cbr\u003ePerfect. From head to toe.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eLara is tough, but she has a big heart. She changes her mind when the truth is presented to her, and is willing to defend her people, both Madririna and Ithicana, and help them. I wanted to yell at her on many occasions, to make her realize that she was in love with Aren, even if she didn't want to accept it. She is not the typical arrogant girl who only talks and doesn't show her strength; Lara shows that she is strong, that she cares and much more.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAren is a cinnamon roll. Don't touch my baby. I love him too much. He cares too much for his people and does not like them to go to war, to die under his watch and reign. He doesn't want a war, but soon gets caught up in one. He is not the typical love interest who is arrogant and unhinged. He is perfect. He's sweet, kind, funny, brave, strong, and even a little clumsy, but his honesty and position make up for it all.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eEven the side characters are cool, funny and adorable. Jor, you're my hero. Nana, I love you so much. Taryn, you fucking deserved better. Ahna, my queen. Marylyn, you deserved that, bitch. Nobody touches my baby Aren.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003cu\u003eRomance.\u003c/u\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003e*chef kiss*\u003cbr\u003eThere's no way to explain how I felt romance in this book, but this gif:\u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1508082172ra/24181144.gif\" width=\"424\" height=\"320\" alt=\"description\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eI was literally freaking out, screaming and crying when Aren said \"I love you\" to Lara, bECAUSE IT'S MEANT TO BE. IT'S TRUE LOVE. THIS \u003cb\u003eTRUE LOVE\u003c/b\u003e. It's so sweet, a slowburn and natural, without being forced; the freaking tension is real.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cb\u003e\n  \u003cu\u003eOverall.\u003c/u\u003e\n\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr\u003eThis goes straight to my \"marry you with paper rings\" shelf. It's a 5 stars rate and a \"I will love you 'til I die\". I can't express how much I loved this book, how got me screaming and jumping on my chair everytime a plot twist appeared, or there was a romantic or action scene.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYup, I'm still freaking out over that ending.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e \u003cimg src=\"https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1619584770ra/31247750.gif\" width=\"500\" height=\"281\" alt=\"description\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eAnd yes, I will read the second one, The Traitor Queen waiting to see my cinnamon roll filled with love, Aren.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1457640839ra/18383809.gif\" width=\"300\" height=\"200\" alt=\"description\" class=\"gr-hostedUserImg\" loading=\"lazy\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003eyOU MUST READ THIS BOOK, NOW.\u003cbr\u003e\u003cbr\u003ethanks for coming to my ted talk.","rating":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A10KEMNOUSJKOY\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v1.GBnO9cdTV3QfRiFpvYtnBQ\"}}"},"likeCount":213,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":28},"User:161765044":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":161765044,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1779337060i/161765044._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":720,"textReviewsCount":72,"name":"jasmine •｡ꪆৎ ˚⋅","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/161765044-jasmine","contributor":null,"id":161765044},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1X06W8SKC5U3M":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1X06W8SKC5U3M"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1X06W8SKC5U3M\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.CeCnfu2hDLOWGucm\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1X06W8SKC5U3M","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1X06W8SKC5U3M"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.CeCnfu2hDLOWGucm","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.CeCnfu2hDLOWGucm"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/161765044?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/6497786311"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.eCs0YUKQ61VzRWExmGdmJg":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.eCs0YUKQ61VzRWExmGdmJg","creator":{"__ref":"User:161765044"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1785773827650,"createdAt":1736407005193,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1740181027106,"text":"⤷2.5! Sadly kind of a big disappointment 😭 The enemies/hidden identities plot is usually fun, but it wasn't very well done in this case... He's already weary that she's a spy but still somehow gave away his trust :') Lara's motives to follow her father was also a bit ridiculous I fear!! They had lots of 'romance building' moments but not a lot of it was good imo... Minor complaint that there's awkward/unfitting lingo in between that kinda made me cringe. Some parts about the bridge was less political intrigue and more on the boring side. Still someeee entertainment mostly through stress and a good plot twist at the end!!!","rating":2,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1X06W8SKC5U3M\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"